{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":113567,"duration_api_ms":112149,"num_turns":18,"result":"## Workflow Knowledge Report Generated\n\nI have successfully analyzed the 1000Genome workflow repository and produced a comprehensive workflow knowledge Markdown file. Here is the complete content:\n\n---\n\n# 1000Genome Workflow Knowledge Report\n\n**Workflow Name:** 1000Genome\n**Framework:** Pegasus WMS v5.0+\n**Analysis Date:** 2026-03-11\n**Agent:** Claude\n\n---\n\n## 1. Repository Structure Overview\n\nThe workflow repository is organized as follows:\n\n```\n1000genome-workflow/\n├── daxgen.py                    # Pegasus DAX generator (workflow definition)\n├── data.csv                     # Input manifest: 10 chromosomes with row counts\n├── env.sh                       # Environment configuration (Decaf/MPI modules)\n├── prepare_input.sh             # Input data preparation script\n├── README.md                    # Documentation\n├── bin/                         # Task executables\n│   ├── individuals.py           # Parse VCF, extract individual mutations\n│   ├── individuals_merge.py     # Merge individual results\n│   ├── sifting.py              # Process SIFT scores\n│   ├── mutation_overlap.py      # Analyze mutation overlaps\n│   ├── frequency.py            # Analyze mutation frequency\n│   └── individuals_mpi.py, etc. # MPI variants (Decaf/PMC mode)\n├── lib/                         # Decaf/Bredala libraries (deployment-specific)\n├── data/\n│   ├── 20130502/              # Input dataset (chromosomes & SIFT annotations)\n│   │   └── sifting/           # SIFT VEP annotation files per chromosome\n│   └── populations/           # Population membership lists (ALL, AFR, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS)\n├── docs/                        # Workflow diagram\n└── analysis/                    # Output analysis directory [unknown contents]\n```\n\n**Entry Point:** `daxgen.py` generates a Pegasus DAX (Directed Acyclic Graph XML) file defining the workflow.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Stages and Tasks\n\nThe workflow consists of **5 task types** organized into **2 main stages: Data Preparation → Analysis**.\n\n### Stage 1: Data Preparation (Per-Chromosome Parallelism)\n\n#### Task 2.1.1: Individuals\n- **Purpose:** Parse VCF files and extract individual-level mutation data per chromosome.\n- **Executables:** `individuals.py` (Python) or `individuals` (bash wrapper)\n- **Inputs:**\n  - `ALL.chr{N}.250000.vcf` - Raw VCF file per chromosome (250,000 variants)\n  - `columns.txt` - Tab-delimited file listing individual IDs (genome column headers)\n- **Parameters:** `{inputfile} {chromosome} {counter} {stop} {total}`\n  - `counter`, `stop`: Line range for job (enables per-chromosome parallelism via `--individuals-jobs` flag)\n  - `total`: Total line count (250,000 per chromosome)\n- **Processing Logic:**\n  - Filters VCF lines by allele frequency (AF): Selects heterozygotes if AF ≥ 0.5, homozygotes if AF < 0.5\n  - For each individual in columns.txt, writes filtered mutations to `chr{N}.{individual_id}` files\n  - Extracts fields: RS number, position (POS), reference (REF), alternate (ALT), allele frequency (AF)\n  - Organizes outputs into per-individual files within a chromosome-specific directory\n- **Output:** `chr{N}n-{counter}-{stop}.tar.gz`\n  - Compressed archive containing individual mutation files\n  - ~2500+ files per archive (one per individual)\n  - Format: TAB-delimited text (RS, POS, REF, ALT, AF)\n\n#### Task 2.1.2: Sifting\n- **Purpose:** Extract SIFT pathogenicity scores from VEP-annotated VCF per chromosome.\n- **Executables:** `sifting.py` (Python) or `sifting` (bash wrapper)\n- **Inputs:**\n  - `ALL.chr{N}.phase3_shapeit2_mvncall_integrated_v5.20130502.sites.annotation.vcf` - VEP-annotated VCF\n- **Parameters:** `{inputfile} {chromosome}`\n- **Processing Logic:**\n  - Extracts VCF header line count (lines starting with '#')\n  - Filters for lines containing \"deleterious\" or \"tolerated\" AND \"rs\" (RS number)\n  - Extracts INFO field (column 8) pipe-delimited: position [4], ENSG ID [16], phenotype [17]\n  - Outputs: line number, RS ID, ENSG ID, SIFT category, phenotype\n- **Output:** `sifted.SIFT.chr{N}.txt`\n  - Format: SPACE-delimited text (line_num, rs_id, ensg_id, sift_pred, phenotype)\n  - Subset of VCF (deleterious/tolerated variants with rs numbers only)\n\n#### Task 2.1.3: Individuals_Merge\n- **Purpose:** Merge per-chunk individual data across multiple parallel Individuals jobs per chromosome.\n- **Executables:** `individuals_merge.py` (Python) or `individuals_merge` (bash wrapper)\n- **Inputs:**\n  - N × `chr{N}n-{counter}-{stop}.tar.gz` files (from Individuals task)\n  - Requires: `(N_rows / chunk_size)` tar files input\n- **Parameters:** `{chromosome} {tar_file1} {tar_file2} ... {tar_fileN}`\n- **Processing Logic:**\n  - Creates temporary directory for each tar archive\n  - Extracts each tar, reads individual mutation files\n  - Merges per-individual files across all tars via dictionary accumulation\n  - Re-compresses merged results\n  - Cleans temporary directories\n- **Output:** `chr{N}n.tar.gz`\n  - Single merged archive per chromosome\n  - Contains consolidated individual mutation files\n\n### Stage 2: Analysis (Per-Chromosome × Population Parallelism)\n\n#### Task 2.2.1: Mutation_Overlap\n- **Purpose:** Measure pairwise mutation overlaps among individuals within a population by chromosome.\n- **Executable:** `mutation_overlap.py`\n- **Inputs:**\n  - `chr{N}n.tar.gz` - Merged individual mutation data (from Individuals_Merge)\n  - `sifted.SIFT.chr{N}.txt` - SIFT scores (from Sifting)\n  - Population file (e.g., `ALL`, `EUR`, `AFR`) - Individual ID list\n  - `columns.txt` - Full genome ID list\n- **Parameters:** `-c {chromosome} -pop {population_file}`\n- **Processing Logic:**\n  - Extracts individual tar archive\n  - Reads population membership and maps to genome IDs\n  - Loads SIFT score annotations\n  - Computes pairwise mutation overlaps (integer counts of shared variants per pair)\n  - Generates overlap matrix and statistical summaries\n  - Produces visualizations (heatmaps, plots)\n- **Output:** `chr{N}-{pop}.tar.gz`\n  - Archive structure: `chr{N}-{pop}/output_no_sift/` + `plots_no_sift/`\n  - Output files: mutation counts, pairwise overlaps, statistics, visualizations\n\n#### Task 2.2.2: Frequency\n- **Purpose:** Analyze mutation frequency distribution using random individual sampling.\n- **Executable:** `frequency.py`\n- **Inputs:**\n  - `chr{N}n.tar.gz` - Merged individual data (same as Mutation_Overlap)\n  - `sifted.SIFT.chr{N}.txt` - SIFT scores (same as Mutation_Overlap)\n  - Population file (e.g., `ALL`, `EUR`)\n  - `columns.txt` - Full genome ID list\n- **Parameters:** `-c {chromosome} -pop {population_file}`\n- **Configuration (hardcoded):**\n  - `n_runs = 1000` - Number of random sampling iterations\n  - `n_indiv = 52` - Size of sampled individual subsets\n- **Processing Logic:**\n  - Extracts individual tar archive\n  - Performs 1000 rounds of random sampling (52 individuals per round)\n  - For each round, counts shared mutations without SIFT filtering\n  - Aggregates overlap frequency distribution\n  - Generates null distribution for statistical significance testing\n  - Produces frequency histograms and summary statistics\n- **Output:** `chr{N}-{pop}-freq.tar.gz`\n  - Archive structure: `chr{N}-{pop}-freq/output_no_sift/` + `plots_no_sift/`\n\n---\n\n## 3. Data Objects Registry\n\n### Input Data Objects\n\n| Name | Format | Source | Description |\n|------|--------|--------|-------------|\n| VCF chromosome file | VCF (tab-delimited) | External / `data/20130502/` | 250K variants per file; contains individual genotypes for 2504 individuals |\n| VEP annotation file | VCF (tab-delimited) | External / `data/20130502/sifting/` | VEP-annotated VCF with SIFT predictions in INFO field |\n| Population file | Text (space-delimited) | `data/populations/{ALL,AFR,AMR,EAS,EUR,GBR,SAS}` | Individual ID lists (7 populations: ALL, AFR, AMR, EAS, EUR, GBR, SAS) |\n| Columns file | Text (tab-delimited) | `data/20130502/columns.txt` | Genome-wide individual ID list (2504 individuals) |\n| Data manifest | CSV | `data.csv` | Specifies 10 chromosomes with row counts and annotation file paths |\n\n### Intermediate Data Objects\n\n| Name | Format | Source | Destination | Description |\n|------|--------|--------|-------------|-------------|\n| Individual chunk archive | TAR.GZ | Individuals | Individuals_Merge | Per-chunk individual mutation data (~2500 files per archive) |\n| Merged individual archive | TAR.GZ | Individuals_Merge | Mutation_Overlap, Frequency | Consolidated individual mutation data per chromosome |\n| SIFT score file | Text (space-delimited) | Sifting | Mutation_Overlap, Frequency | Variant-level SIFT annotations; deleterious/tolerated variants only |\n\n### Output Data Objects\n\n| Name | Format | Source | Description |\n|------|--------|--------|-------------|\n| Mutation overlap archive | TAR.GZ | Mutation_Overlap | Pairwise mutation overlap statistics per population per chromosome |\n| Frequency archive | TAR.GZ | Frequency | Null distribution from random sampling per population per chromosome |\n| Visualizations | PNG | Mutation_Overlap, Frequency | Matplotlib heatmaps and plots |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Producer-Consumer Dependencies\n\n```\nIndividuals (N chunks per chromosome)\n  └─→ Individuals_Merge (1 per chromosome)\n  \nSifting (1 per chromosome, runs in parallel)\n\nIndividuals_Merge & Sifting outputs consumed by:\n  ├─→ Mutation_Overlap (7 populations × 10 chromosomes = 70 tasks)\n  └─→ Frequency (7 populations × 10 chromosomes = 70 tasks)\n```\n\n**Edge Types:**\n- **Merge:** N:1 reduction (Individuals → Individuals_Merge)\n- **Fan-out:** 1:7 expansion (Individuals_Merge → 7 analysis tasks per chromosome)\n- **Leaf:** No downstream consumers (Mutation_Overlap, Frequency are outputs)\n\n---\n\n## 5. Workflow Structure and Pattern\n\n**Overall Pattern:** Multi-Level Parallel Pipeline with Fan-Out\n\n```\nLevel 1: Per-Chromosome Parallelism (10 chromosomes in parallel)\n├─ Individuals (chunks per chromosome)\n│  └─ Individuals_Merge (1 per chromosome)\n│     └─ [Sifting (1 per chromosome) in parallel]\n│\nLevel 2: Per-Chromosome × Per-Population Analysis (fan-out)\n├─ Mutation_Overlap (70 tasks total)\n└─ Frequency (70 tasks total)\n```\n\n**DAG Properties:**\n- Strictly acyclic (linear flow with fan-out)\n- 3 dependency stages\n- 10 chromosomes × (1 Merge + 1 Sifting + 7 Analysis pairs) ≈ 140 logical task groups\n\n---\n\n## 6. I/O Behavioral Hints\n\n- **Small-File Overhead:** ~2500 individual mutation files per chromosome; mitigated by tar.gz bundling\n- **Data Reuse:** Mutation_Overlap and Frequency share same inputs (merged individuals, SIFT scores)\n- **Format Conversions:** VCF → text files → tar.gz → extraction (multiple serialization steps)\n- **Compute-Intensive Analysis:** O(n²) pairwise comparisons + 1000 random sampling iterations\n- **Selective Filtering:** VCF allele frequency filtering reduces per-individual file sizes\n- **Known Cardinality:** Fixed 10 chromosomes, 7 populations, 2504 individuals (no dynamic discovery)\n\n---\n\n## 7. Summary\n\nThe **1000Genome workflow** analyzes genomic variation across populations:\n1. **Parses** VCF variant data per chromosome in parallel\n2. **Extracts** individual mutation calls and pathogenicity scores (SIFT)\n3. **Merges** individual results across parallel chunks per chromosome\n4. **Analyzes** pairwise mutation overlaps and frequency distributions per chromosome × population\n\n**Data Scale:** ~2500 individuals × 250K variants per chromosome; outputs are statistical summaries and visualizations.\n\n---\n\nSTATUS: success | OUTPUT: /home/mtang11/scripts/workflow-representation-description/workflow_knowledge/1000genome-knowledge-claude-trial1.md","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"d0e1711b-56ff-420b-bbcf-7cb964572f09","total_cost_usd":0.15935145,"usage":